          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Goerss-Hopkins-Miller theorem
            (
            %a{:href => "#GoerssHopkinsA"}> Goerss-Hopkins A
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GoerssHopkinsB"} Goerss-Hopkins B
            %em Goerss-Hopkins-Miller-Lurie theorem
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"}> Lurie (Survey)
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Representability+Theorems"} Lurie (Representability)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+curve"} elliptic curve
            of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/elliptic+cohomology"} elliptic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
            lifts in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherence"} coherent
            way to an assignment of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} representing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            regarded as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mi der
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{M}^{der}}
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack+of+elliptic+curves"} moduli stack of elliptic curves
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+algebraic+geometry"} derived algebraic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+scheme"} derived scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mi der
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}^{der}
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+geometry"} E-∞ geometry
            (“spectral geometry”) This is sketched in (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"}> Lurie
            ) and discussed in detail in (
            %a{:href => "#Behrens13"}> Behrens 13
            ).
          %p
            In detail the theorem utilizes and establishes more general tools concerning the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/obstruction"} obstruction
            theory of lifting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group+laws"} formal group laws
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theories"} cohomology theories
            and homotopy associative/commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+rings"} A-∞ rings
            and to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            structure, respectively.
          %p
            In the succinct and suggestive form of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"}> Lurie, theorem 1.1
            ) the Goerss-Hopkins-Miller theorem leads the existence of the lift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mi top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{M}^{top}}
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mn ∞
                          %mi Rings
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
