          %h2#references References
          %p An introduction to and survey of the Goerss-Hopkins-Miller-Lurie theorem is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
              ,
              %em Topological modular forms (after Hopkins, Miller, and Lurie)
              Séminaire BOURBAKI Mars 2009 61ème année, 2008-2009, no 1005(2009)(
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.5130"}> arXiv:0910.5130
              )
          %p which has grown out of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Topological+Algebraic+Geometry+-+A+Workshop"}> Topological Algebraic Geometry - A Workshop
                  \.
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/people/grk1150/Past_Events/AG-programm-SS07.pdf"} pdf
          %p Details on the Hopkins-Miller theorem are in
          %ul
            %li#Rezk97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notes on the Hopkins-Miller theorem
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/~rezk/hopkins-miller-thm.pdf"} pdf
          %p and a survey is also in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akhil+Mathew"}> Akhil Mathew
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://amathew.wordpress.com/tag/hopkins-miller-theorem/"} Hopkins-Miller theorem I
          %p The Goerss-Hopkins theorem is laid out in
          %ul
            %li#GoerssHopkinsA
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Moduli spaces of commutative ring spectra
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Structured ring spectra
              %p
                Math. Soc. Lecture Note Ser., vol. 315, Cambridge Univ. Press, Cambridge, 2004, pp. 151-200. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.northwestern.edu/~pgoerss/papers/sum.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511529955.009"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511529955.009
            %li#GoerssHopkinsB
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
                %em Moduli problems for structured ring spectra
                (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.northwestern.edu/~pgoerss/spectra/obstruct.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            The actual details of the application of the Goerss-Hopkins-Miller theorem to the construction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mi der
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{\mathcal{M}^{der}}
            (and hence of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tmf"} tmf
          %ul
            %li#Behrens13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+Behrens"}> Mark Behrens
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Notes on the construction of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi tmf
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} tmf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.mit.edu/~mbehrens/papers/buildTMF.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            An exposition with indications of further developments in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+theory"} (infinity,1)-category theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aaron+Mazel-Gee"}> Aaron Mazel-Gee
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Goerss-Hopkins obstruction theory for
                  = succeed "-categories" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn ∞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~aaron/writing/thursday-cghost-beamer.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a{:href => "A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology#gluingallellipticcohomologytheoriestothetmfspectrum"} survey of elliptic curves – Gluing of curves to a spectrum
          %p A more abstract formulation of this is sketched in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A+Survey+of+Elliptic+Cohomology"} A Survey of Elliptic Cohomology
          %p with technical details in a sequence of articles, including
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Formal+Moduli+Problems+and+DG-Lie+Algebras"} Moduli problems for ring spectra
                (
                %a{:href => "https://people.math.rochester.edu/faculty/doug/otherpapers/goerss-hopkins.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Representability+Theorems"} Representability Theorems
